('PUT-FA-01','golf_drill','Chalk-Line Face Set','Putting · Face Alignment','Learn','Chalk-Line Face Set develops aiming the putter face accurately at address through a specific, measurable putting task.','Create a visible intended start line and a perpendicular face reference at the ball. Use one ball and rebuild the setup each time. For Chalk-Line Face Set, use station variation 1: flat line.','1. Read from behind the ball. 2. Select a precise start-line point. 3. Set the putter face at that point before building the stance. 4. Verify the face against the drill reference, then putt without redirecting it.','Aim the face first and organise the body around the chosen face direction.','Putter, ball, tees and the alignment reference named in the drill','Complete 10 independent aim-and-putt routines.','The face matches the intended reference on at least 8 of 10 setups.','Remove the reference before striking or use changing breaking putts.','Use a straight one-metre putt and keep the reference visible.','Vector Putting Drill Library · 120 Drill Collection','approved'),
