('PUT-SQ-01','golf_drill','Impact-Tee Face Gate','Putting · Square Face at Impact','Learn','Impact-Tee Face Gate develops returning the putter face squarely at impact through a specific, measurable putting task.','Create a start-line gate 15–30 cm beyond the ball and a square face reference at address. Begin from short range. For Impact-Tee Face Gate, use station variation 1: flat line.','1. Aim through the centre of the gate. 2. Make the rehearsal specified by the drill title. 3. Strike the centre of the ball and hold the finish. 4. Score only whether the ball starts through the gate, then reset.','Return the putter face squarely at impact so the ball launches on the selected start line.','Putter, balls, tees and square-face reference','Complete 2 sets of 10 putts.','At least 16 of 20 balls pass cleanly through the start gate.','Narrow the gate, move it closer or add a breaking start line.','Widen the gate and shorten the putt.','Vector Putting Drill Library · 120 Drill Collection','approved'),
('PUT-SQ-02','golf_drill','Ball-Start-Line Gate','Putting · Square Face at Impact','Calibrate','Ball-Start-Line Gate develops returning the putter face squarely at impact through a specific, measurable putting task.','Create a start-line gate 15–30 cm beyond the ball and a square face reference at address. Begin from short range. For Ball-Start-Line Gate, use station variation 2: uphill line.','1. Aim through the centre of the gate. 2. Make the rehearsal specified by the drill title. 3. Strike the centre of the ball and hold the finish. 4. Score only whether the ball starts through the gate, then reset.','Return the putter face squarely at impact so the ball launches on the selected start line.','Putter, balls, tees and square-face reference','Complete 2 sets of 10 putts.','At least 16 of 20 balls pass cleanly through the start gate.','Narrow the gate, move it closer or add a breaking start line.','Widen the gate and shorten the putt.','Vector Putting Drill Library · 120 Drill Collection','approved'),
('PUT-SQ-03','golf_drill','Ruler Roll-Off','Putting · Square Face at Impact','Transfer','Ruler Roll-Off develops returning the putter face squarely at impact through a specific, measurable putting task.','Create a start-line gate 15–30 cm beyond the ball and a square face reference at address. Begin from short range. For Ruler Roll-Off, use station variation 3: downhill line.','1. Aim through the centre of the gate. 2. Make the rehearsal specified by the drill title. 3. Strike the centre of the ball and hold the finish. 4. Score only whether the ball starts through the gate, then reset.','Return the putter face squarely at impact so the ball launches on the selected start line.','Putter, balls, tees and square-face reference','Complete 2 sets of 10 putts.','At least 16 of 20 balls pass cleanly through the start gate.','Narrow the gate, move it closer or add a breaking start line.','Widen the gate and shorten the putt.','Vector Putting Drill Library · 120 Drill Collection','approved'),
