('PUT-CP-01','golf_drill','Twin-Rail Path','Putting · Club Path','Learn','Twin-Rail Path develops moving the putter on a repeatable intended path through a specific, measurable putting task.','Build the path station named in the drill using tees, rails, string or an arc reference. Centre the putter with clear space to move. For Twin-Rail Path, use station variation 1: flat line.','1. Make two slow rehearsals through the path station. 2. Add a ball without changing the motion. 3. Move the putter through the backstroke and follow-through references without contact. 4. Hold the finish, score the path and reset.','Move the putter on a repeatable intended route without steering it around the station.','Putter, balls and the path aid named in the drill','Complete 3 sets of 6 strokes.','At least 15 of 18 strokes clear the path station and meet the start-line standard.','Narrow the channel, extend stroke length or remove one visual reference.','Widen the channel and use a shorter stroke.','Vector Putting Drill Library · 120 Drill Collection','approved'),
